        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "FOR SALE BY PRIVATE TREATY\n2C AYLMER ROAD, NEWCASTLE, CO DUBLIN. D22 XH90.\n\nTo organize a viewing or to place a bid on this property go to www.teamlorraine.ie or scan the QR code on the photograph section of this brochure.\n\n`Circle of Legends` & National RE/MAX Award-winning agent, Team Lorraine Mulligan of RE/MAX Results welcomes you to this superb opportunity to purchase this fabulous 4 bedroomed family home with an attic conversion in the heart of Newcastle Village. This home boasts several upgrades including a gas boiler being only two years old allowing the BER to be an impressive B rating. On arrival you will note the generous sized garden giving parking for up to two cars. The main hall is of a generous proportion with the main reception room is both bright and airy and boasts shutters on the winders and an open fireplace which will give all the calls for a cozy warm space during the winter months. At the rear of the property is a large kitchen, dining and utility space with wonderful solid oak cabinetry, island and solid wooden floors throughout. This room epitomises the heart of the family. The low maintenance rear south facing garden allows the discerning buyer bringing the indoors out during those long summer evenings with dining alfresco of just shooting the breeze. This space also boasts a large shed for storage. A guest W.C. completes the ground-floor accommodation. On the first floor, there are four generously sized bedrooms, with the primary bedroom benefiting from an en-suite, along with a main family bathroom. The property also enjoys the added benefit of an attic conversion, providing valuable additional space and featuring its own en-suite.\n\nThis is truly an ideal home for that growing family and being set in the heart of the village is pivotal to all local amenities including Schools, Creches, SuperValu, Lidl/ bars and restaurants. \n\nCondition & Possession\nThis home is excellently presented and fully habitable. This property is also very versatile and presents an exciting opportunity for buyers to put their own stamp on this delightful home it and build equity in the process.\n\nAccommodation\nThe downstairs accommodation consists of a hallway, sitting room, and a kitchen/dining area that overlooks the sunny back garden. Utility room and guest W.C. Upstairs enjoys four bedrooms primary ensuite, main bathroom, and attic space.\n\nAbout the Area Newcastle Co Dublin\nNewcastle is one of southwest Dublin`s most established residential villages and is situated approximately 16 km from Dublin city centre on the south bank of the River Liffey. It is a community with genuine character a vibrant mix of long-standing families and newer residents drawn by new homes being built in the area, excellent amenities, a strong sense of neighbourhood, and outstanding connectivity. Including just a moments` walk to the 68-bus stop to Dublin or the W6 which will drop you at the Luas in one direction and both Hazelhatch/ Maynooth Train lines and Maynooth University in the other. This home is ideally located for the M7/M4M50 Dublin Airport\n\n\nDON`T MISS THIS OPPORTUNITY TO VIEW THIS SUPERB PIECE OF REAL ESTATE IN AN UNBEATABLE LOCATION. \nVIEWINGS HIGHLY RECOMMENDED. INTEREST IS SURE TO BE STRONG\n"
      },
